"hours (hair salon, hospital etc.)</b>\", the prices of services (and service "
"options) are calculated by combining the price levels configured in the "
"\"<b>Services</b>\" tab (\"<b>Base Price</b>\" to \"<b>Price 6</b>\") with "
"the \"<b>Applicable Price Level</b>\" and \"<b>Enable Quantity-Based Price "
"Adjustment for Services</b>\" settings configured for each guest item in the "
"\"<b>Guests</b>\" tab."
msgstr ""

#: /var/www/html/wp/wp-content/plugins/booking-package/lib/Documents.php:25
msgid ""
"1. Calculation Rules Based on \"Enable Quantity-Based Price Adjustment for "
"Services\""
msgstr ""

#: /var/www/html/wp/wp-content/plugins/booking-package/lib/Documents.php:26
msgid ""
"Depending on the configuration of your active guest items, service prices "
"are calculated using one of the following three patterns:"
msgstr ""

#: /var/www/html/wp/wp-content/plugins/booking-package/lib/Documents.php:28
msgid ""
"Pattern A: When ALL Guest Items Are Set to \"Enabled\" (Proportional Per-"
"Guest Pricing Model)"
msgstr ""

#: /var/www/html/wp/wp-content/plugins/booking-package/lib/Documents.php:29
msgid ""
"The service price is calculated solely from the sum of \"<b>(Unit price of "
"the Applicable Price Level) &times; (Number of Guests selected)</b>\" for "
"each guest item."
msgstr ""

#: /var/www/html/wp/wp-content/plugins/booking-package/lib/Documents.php:30
msgid ""
"<b>Example</b>: If \"Adults\" (\"<b>Applicable Price Level</b>\": \"<b>Base "
"Price</b>\" = $100, \"<b>Enable Quantity-Based Price Adjustment for "
"Services</b>\": \"<b>Enabled</b>\") is selected with a quantity of 2, the "
"service price is $100 &times; 2 = $200."
msgstr ""

#: /var/www/html/wp/wp-content/plugins/booking-package/lib/Documents.php:31
msgid ""
"<b>How to Configure a Free ($0) Guest Category (e.g., Infants or Observers)</"
"b>: Even if you do not want a specific guest item to add to the service "
"price, set \"<b>Enable Quantity-Based Price Adjustment for Services</b>\" to "
"\"<b>Enabled</b>\" for that guest item as well. Then, under \"<b>Applicable "
"Price Level</b>\", select a price level that is set to <code>0</code> in the "
"\"<b>Services</b>\" tab (such as \"<b>Price 2</b>\" or \"<b>Price 3</b>\")."
msgstr ""

#: /var/www/html/wp/wp-content/plugins/booking-package/lib/Documents.php:33
msgid ""
"Pattern B: When \"Disabled\" and \"Enabled\" Guest Items Are Mixed (Fixed "
"Base Price + Additional Guest Pricing Model)"
msgstr ""

#: /var/www/html/wp/wp-content/plugins/booking-package/lib/Documents.php:34
msgid ""
"When guest items set to \"<b>Disabled</b>\" and guest items set to "
"\"<b>Enabled</b>\" for \"<b>Enable Quantity-Based Price Adjustment for "
"Services</b>\" coexist, the total service price is calculated by combining "
"both as follows:"
msgstr ""

#: /var/www/html/wp/wp-content/plugins/booking-package/lib/Documents.php:35
msgid ""
"If at least one active guest item is set to \"<b>Disabled</b>\", <b>one unit "
"of the service's \"Base Price\" is always charged as a fixed base fee</b>, "
"regardless of the number of guests selected for that item (even if left "
"unselected or set to 0)."
msgstr ""

#: /var/www/html/wp/wp-content/plugins/booking-package/lib/Documents.php:36
msgid ""
"When 1 or more guests are selected for any guest item set to \"<b>Enabled</"
"b>\", their \"<b>(Unit price of the Applicable Price Level) &times; (Number "
"of Guests selected)</b>\" is <b>added on top of the fixed \"Base Price\"</b>."
msgstr ""

#: /var/www/html/wp/wp-content/plugins/booking-package/lib/Documents.php:37
msgid ""
"<b>Use Case</b>: Ideal for studio rentals or private lessons where a fixed "
"base fee applies for the primary representative (\"<b>Disabled</b>\": "
"guarantees 1 unit of \"<b>Base Price</b>\", e.g., $100) and an additional "
"per-person fee applies only when companions are added (\"<b>Enabled</b>\": "
"e.g., \"<b>Price 2</b>\" = $20 per additional guest)."
msgstr ""

#: /var/www/html/wp/wp-content/plugins/booking-package/lib/Documents.php:38
msgid ""
"<b>Important Note</b>: When registering multiple guest items such as "
"\"Adults (\"<b>Enabled</b>\")\" and \"Children (Free)\", if you set the "
"\"Children\" guest item to \"<b>Disabled</b>\", one unit of the \"<b>Base "
"Price</b>\" will be added as a fixed base fee in addition to the per-person "
"charge for \"Adults\" (resulting in a total equivalent to \"selected number "
"of guests + 1\"). If you want to calculate the price strictly based on the "
"selected number of guests, please follow <b>Pattern A</b> by setting all "
"guest items to \"<b>Enabled</b>\" and assigning a price level of <code>0</"
"code> to free guest categories."
msgstr ""

#: /var/www/html/wp/wp-content/plugins/booking-package/lib/Documents.php:40
msgid ""
"Pattern C: When ALL Guest Items Are Set to \"Disabled\" (Flat-Rate Per-"
"Booking Model)"
msgstr ""

#: /var/www/html/wp/wp-content/plugins/booking-package/lib/Documents.php:41
msgid ""
"The service price is not multiplied by the number of guests. Regardless of "
"how many guests are selected, only <b>one unit of the service's \"Base "
"Price\"</b> is charged per booking."
msgstr ""

#: /var/www/html/wp/wp-content/plugins/booking-package/lib/Documents.php:43
msgid "2. Other Guest-Related Pricing and Capacity Settings"
msgstr ""

#: /var/www/html/wp/wp-content/plugins/booking-package/lib/Documents.php:44
msgid ""
"<b>\"Extra Charge\" in Guest \"Options\"</b>: The \"<b>Extra Charge</b>\" "
"configured in the \"<b>Options</b>\" table at the bottom of each guest "
"item's edit screen is not multiplied by the \"<b>Number of Guests</b>\". "
"Instead, the exact amount configured for the selected option is added "
"directly to the total amount."
msgstr ""

#: /var/www/html/wp/wp-content/plugins/booking-package/lib/Documents.php:45
msgid ""
"<b>\"Enable Quantity-Based Price Adjustment for Extra Charges\"</b>: When "
"set to \"<b>Enabled</b>\", the unit amount of any \"<b>Extra Charge</b>\" "
"registered under the \"<b>Extra Charges | Taxes</b>\" tab is multiplied by "
"the total number of guests selected across all guest items that have this "
"setting \"<b>Enabled</b>\" (if the total selected number of target guests is "
"0, or if all guest items are set to \"<b>Disabled</b>\", the \"<b>Extra "
"Charge</b>\" is applied once per booking)."
msgstr ""

#: /var/www/html/wp/wp-content/plugins/booking-package/lib/Documents.php:46
msgid "\"Count Total Guests Toward Availability\""
msgstr ""

#: /var/www/html/wp/wp-content/plugins/booking-package/lib/Documents.php:47
msgid ""
"<b>\"Included\"</b>: The selected \"<b>Number of Guests</b>\" is deducted "
"from the time slot's \"<b>Remaining Slots</b>\" (\"<b>Available Slots</"
"b>\"). If at least one active guest item is set to \"<b>Included</b>\", the "
"customer must select a total of at least 1 guest across the \"<b>Included</"
"b>\" guest items to complete a booking."
msgstr ""

#: /var/www/html/wp/wp-content/plugins/booking-package/lib/Documents.php:48
msgid ""
"<b>\"Excluded\"</b>: The selected \"<b>Number of Guests</b>\" is not "
"deducted from the time slot's \"<b>Remaining Slots</b>\". If all active "
"guest items are set to \"<b>Excluded</b>\", a booking can be completed even "
"when 0 guests are selected, consuming 1 slot for the booker themselves."
msgstr ""

